{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/905969-slashers-compared-to-heroes","id":905969,"title":"Slashers Compared to Heroes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-02T14:48:12-07:00","id":905969,"title":"Slashers Compared to Heroes?","content":"What does this mean for our lovable psychopaths?<br /> <br /> <br /> From what I remember, Heroes are the things that Hunters are afraid of becoming, yet Slashers are described as Hunters that were pushed too far and just kind of snapped in one form or another.<br /> <br /> So how does one differentiate between a Hero and a Slasher, or how is one path chosen over the other? Are Slashers even still prevalent anymore, or have they been tossed out in favor of Heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:51:38-07:00","id":905971,"title":"","content":"Slashers are insane to the point of supernatural endowment; Heroes retain their higher functions, albeit with an obsessive bent that can only be born from psychic abuse, repeated or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:54:26-07:00","id":905974,"title":"","content":"That and being a Hero is at least somewhat intrinsic, where it's hard to tell if the possibility to become a Slasher is any more inherent than the potential to turn into a 'regular' serial killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-02-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:56:05-07:00","id":905977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/905969-slashers-compared-to-heroes?p=905971#post905971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slashers are insane to the point of supernatural endowment; Heroes retain their higher functions, albeit with an obsessive bent that can only be born from psychic abuse, repeated or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's only the Heroes whose souls were weak and damaged enough to let the Monomyth seep into the cracks and twist them. Heroes with high Integrity are honestly good people, for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:15:15-07:00","id":905993,"title":"","content":"I see, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:24:22-07:00","id":906001,"title":"","content":"They're also not mutually exclusive. With a Hero losing all of his integrity easily becoming a slasher, maybe focused on Beasts and the people around them. (for example the slasher will kill anyone the Beast has fed from).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T15:03:49-07:00","id":907296,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine actually summed it up quite well for me when the topic came up during a closing shift.<br /> <br /> Heroes are people who have a hole inside of them that the Hero's Journey fills with a purpose. <br /> <br /> Slashers are whole individuals, they're just so alien on the inside that they might as well be a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:07:45-07:00","id":907355,"title":"","content":"I think the main difference is that Heroes live for the spectacle surrounding their perceived victory. They want to be in the spotlight, shout to the heavens about how awful the Beast is and how righteous they are for slaying it. There's a chance that they'll let the Beast go if there's no audience or if the Beast has managed to make the Hero look bad to the witnesses. It's more of a game than a true Quest, and from the Hero's perspective, it's always personal and justified.<br /> <br /> Slashers are more concerned with the act of murder itself, and they can be more subtle and adaptive. They often possess mental conditions that cloud their judgement, but until they become Scourges, I'd say there isn't a metaphysical narrative force pulling their strings. Their desire to take lives comes from within.<br /> <br /> It's not always so clearly defined, of course. There's some overlap between Heroes and Legend Slashers. A few Heroes can be Byronic, and maybe even put down the sword someday. Whether it is easier for a Hero or a Slasher to reform should be analyzed on an individual basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:39:39-07:00","id":907368,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong; but aren't Heroes <i>inherently</i> low-Integrity? As in, if they ever raise their Integrity above a given threshold, they cease to be Heroes? <br /> <br /> I know that in 1e, Slashers were similarly low Morality; but I don't know if that still holds true with 2e's shift from Morality to Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:43:44-07:00","id":907372,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure you're thinking of the first draft, if anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:50:31-07:00","id":907373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/905969-slashers-compared-to-heroes?p=907368#post907368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong; but aren't Heroes <i>inherently</i> low-Integrity? As in, if they ever raise their Integrity above a given threshold, they cease to be Heroes? <br /> <br /> I know that in 1e, Slashers were similarly low Morality; but I don't know if that still holds true with 2e's shift from Morality to Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's less &quot;all Heroes are low Integrity&quot; so much as &quot;all Heroes <i>who act like Heroes as opposed to being normal people with a sense for the Dream</i> are low Integrity&quot;, at least in the published book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T01:09:37-07:00","id":907514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/905969-slashers-compared-to-heroes?p=907373#post907373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it's less &quot;all Heroes are low Integrity&quot; so much as &quot;all Heroes <i>who act like Heroes as opposed to being normal people with a sense for the Dream</i> are low Integrity&quot;, at least in the published book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's the way it is now. In the first draft heroes had to be integrity 4 or lower, now it's just lower integrity heroes are misinterpreting their role in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T01:10:47-07:00","id":907515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/905969-slashers-compared-to-heroes?p=907368#post907368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong; but aren't Heroes <i>inherently</i> low-Integrity? As in, if they ever raise their Integrity above a given threshold, they cease to be Heroes?<br /> <br /> I know that in 1e, Slashers were similarly low Morality; but I don't know if that still holds true with 2e's shift from Morality to Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it makes a lot of sense for slashers to be super low on integrity, it takes a rather broken soul to be so insane that they become a horror movie villain in that fashion. Especially with the mask undertaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T20:10:37-07:00","id":908065,"title":"","content":"For now, Onyx Path is leaving things deliberately vague. There's clearly some overlap, but in-game no one knows why (prompting a lot of speculation by characters). Beasts can claim Kinship with Slashers (as if they were supernatural monsters), but not hunters, for example. And many hunters initially find themselves sympathizing with Heroes, seeing them as kindred spirits . . . at least until the Heroes try to burn down an orphanage to get at a Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/905969-slashers-compared-to-heroes?p=907368#post907368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong; but aren't Heroes <i>inherently</i> low-Integrity? As in, if they ever raise their Integrity above a given threshold, they cease to be Heroes?<br /> <br /> I know that in 1e, Slashers were similarly low Morality; but I don't know if that still holds true with 2e's shift from Morality to Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the others pointed out, not anymore. The final draft clearly has an eye on introducing Heroes as a playable splat in the future. Of course, the average Beast may not know that there are relatively sane Heroes out there - they tend to run into the crazed serial killer far more often <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}